{"id":"makkedah","name":"Makkedah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:makkedah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Makkedah","text":"Herdsman’s place, one of the royal cities of the Canaanites (Josh. 12:16), near which was a cave where the five kings who had confederated against Israel sought refuge (10:10-29). They were put to death by Joshua, who afterwards suspended their bodies upon five trees. It has been identified with the modern village called Sumeil, standing on a low hill about 7 miles to the north-west of Eleutheropolis (Beit Jibrin), where are ancient remains and a great cave. The Palestine Exploration surveyors have, however, identified it with el-Mughar, or “the caves,” 3 miles from Jabneh and 2 1/2 southwest of Ekron, because, they say, “at this site only of all possible sites for Makkedah in the Palestine plain do caves still exist.” (See ADONI-ZEDEC.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","xlit":"Yᵉhôwshûwaʻ","gloss":"Jehoshua , the Jewish leader","kjv":"Jehoshua, Jehoshuah, Joshua","count":10,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H4719","lemma":"מַקֵּדָה","xlit":"Maqqêdâh","gloss":"Makkedah, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Makkedah","count":5,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H4631","lemma":"מְעָרָה","xlit":"mᵉʻârâh","gloss":"a cavern","kjv":"cave, den, hole","count":6,"share":0.4},{"strong":"H2568","lemma":"חָמֵשׁ","xlit":"châmêsh","gloss":"five","kjv":"fif, fifth, five","count":6,"share":0.4},{"strong":"H2244","lemma":"חָבָא","xlit":"châbâʼ","gloss":"to secrete","kjv":"held, hide, do secretly","count":3,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H3412","lemma":"יַרְמוּת","xlit":"Yarmûwth","gloss":"Jarmuth, the name of two places in Palestine","kjv":"Jarmuth","count":2,"share":0.13}],"verses":["Josh.10.17","Josh.10.18","Josh.10.20","Josh.10.21","Josh.10.22","Josh.10.24","Josh.10.25","Josh.10.26","Josh.10.27","Josh.10.28","Josh.10.5","Josh.10.16","Josh.10.19","Josh.10.23","Josh.12.16"],"related":[{"id":"adoni-zedek","type":"cooccur","shar